arch letter
name Municipal Order of Darcap pt. 1/2
msg
Municipal Order of Darcap
Sealed by Authority of the Dual Guilds
Filed in the Black Ledger, Volume IX

Regarding the Catastrophe at Valleynoy, the Dissolution of Its Charter, and the Prohibition of Recovery Efforts

Issued in the Year 6942 EK
Ratified jointly by
The Guild of the Poisoned Dagger
and
The Guild of the Smoking Cauldron

Let it be recorded, without embellishment and without omission, that the settlement known as Valleynoy, founded as a distant outpost of Darcap in cooperation with the City of Navar, has suffered a terminal event resulting in the total loss of population, infrastructure, and civic continuity.

Valleynoy was established for a singular purpose: the development, instruction, and refinement of the Artificer discipline, a sanctioned craft permitting the application of complex magical recipes to armor, weapons, and jewelry. Its students were selected from Darcap and Navar alike. Its laboratories were regulated, though not constrained. Its success was considerable. Its failure was absolute.

On the final day of contact, no distress signal was received. No warning preceded the event. When scheduled transmissions ceased, an inquiry was authorized under standard isolation protocols. That inquiry returned no survivors, no recoverable remains, and no stable arcane signatures consistent with life, death, or undeath.

Valleynoy is not ruined. It is absent.

In response, the following orders are enacted and are to be enforced without exception.

I. Dissolution of Charter

The municipal charter of Valleynoy is hereby revoked. The settlement is declared legally nonexistent. All trade agreements, training accreditations, and intercity obligations tied to Valleynoy are nullified retroactively to the date of its founding.

Artificer certifications issued exclusively through Valleynoy are to be considered incomplete but not invalid. Holders will not be punished. However, no further credentials may be issued under its authority.

II. Destruction and Sealing of Records

All maps, star-charts, ley notations, travel journals, and navigational instructions that indicate the location of Valleynoy are to be surrendered to the Guild of the Poisoned Dagger within fourteen days of this order's circulation.

Unauthorized possession thereafter will be treated as intent to trespass into a prohibited zone.

Records deemed essential to the continuity of Artificer knowledge will be redacted, rewritten, or recontextualized so that no spatial inference may be reconstructed. What can be preserved will be preserved. What cannot will be destroyed.

Memory is not a neutral act.

III. Prohibition of Recovery Expeditions

No sanctioned expedition, civilian, guild, academic, or military, is permitted to seek Valleynoy.

This includes attempts motivated by rescue, recovery of artifacts, reclamation of research, or confirmation of rumors. The absence observed is not stable. Preliminary divinations suggest recursive displacement, conceptual overlap, and phenomena consistent with catastrophic misapplication of Artificer synthesis.

To enter such a space without preparation would be to compound the loss.

To enter it with preparation would be to risk repetition.

IV. On the Navarian Tower

It is acknowledged that multiple witnesses, independent and uncoordinated, report the sighting of the Navarian Tower to the north of where Valleynoy is believed to have existed. The tower is described as extending beyond visual termination, as though descending from the sky and tethered to the ground.

This observation is neither confirmed nor denied.

No attempt is to be made to triangulate Valleynoy's former location using the tower as reference. The tower predates Valleynoy. It will outlast this order. Correlation is not causation, and speculation is not policy.
endmsg
